TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a scope enum, plus `[ClassConstructor]` for DI. Here's each scope:

---

### 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup(TestContext context) { /* ... */ }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

These run for **each** `[Test]` in the class. They must be instance methods (non-static) in the test class.

---

### 2. Once Per Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class IntegrationTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void StartFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://localhost:5000") };
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task HealthCheck() { /* use _client */ }
}
```

These must be **`static`** and take `ClassHookContext`. Runs once before the first / after the last test in the class.

---

### 3. Once Per Assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Start(port: 9090);
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

The class doesn't need `[Test]` methods — TUnit discovers these hooks by attribute. Must be **`static`**, takes `AssemblyHookContext`.

---

### 4. Once Per Entire Test Session

```csharp
public class SessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        using var db = new AppDbContext();
        db.Database.Migrate();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        using var db = new AppDbContext();
        db.Database.EnsureDeleted();
    }
}
```

Must be **`static`**, takes `TestSessionContext`. Runs once for the whole process — even if multiple assemblies are loaded.

---

### Quick Reference

| Scope | Attribute | Static? | Context parameter |
|---|---|---|---|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | **No** (instance) | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes | `TestSessionContext` |

All hook methods can be `async Task` if needed. The `Before`/`After` enum values come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or qualify as `HookType.Test`, etc.).
